From: ppptran <ppptran86@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: yt921x: latch forced SerDes link on AN edge

Vendor HAL programs the SERDES force value first and raises AN_LINK_EN
afterwards; the MAC latches the forced link on that 0->1 edge. Mirror
that order for the external (CPU) port so PORT_STATUS reports link,
needed when the CPU lane runs 2500BASE-X.

Ported to the v6.19 single-file driver used by wf810df-fw from
michioxd/openwrt-wf810df 995-net-dsa-yt921x-latch-force-link-after-serdes.

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x.c
@@ -2234,6 +2234,15 @@
 		res = yt921x_reg_write(priv, YT921X_MDIO_POLLINGn(port), ctrl);
 		if (res)
 			return res;
+
+		/* Vendor HAL forces the SERDES link first, then raises
+		 * AN_LINK_EN; the MAC latches the forced link on that 0->1
+		 * edge (ppptran, michioxd/openwrt-wf810df 995).
+		 */
+		res = yt921x_reg_set_bits(priv, YT921X_PORTn_CTRL(port),
+					  YT921X_PORT_LINK);
+		if (res)
+			return res;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
